{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QrkaGUiwUQDokYho8eyGGC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D17 seen vs. D18+ candidates)\n2\t\n3\tUpdated 2026-10-17 after D17 (1139 ids, 127 members; D17 added AutoHotkey `.ahk`, all modes first try, single T+13 s); gaps\n4\tre-queued 2026-10-18 after the D17-night prebuild (7 built, 1 given up, 1 pending retry). Read with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\n5\tactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\n6\thave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n7\t\n8\tContext that drives the likelihood column:\n9\t- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n10\t  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n11\t  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n12\t  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n13\t  The carried solver (`challenges/day17/scripting-fetch-quest/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n14\t  `analyse_v3`; ran unchanged D9-D17) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, on one line, peelable by hex/base64/\n15\t  reverse within 3 layers. The real D18+ risk is not a new language — it is a new **carrier/encoding/container**, a\n16\t  new **synthetic-label family** (D2-D7 era), or a **GM label-regime flip** on an old one (D15 pool-keyed, D16 date-keyed\n17\t  batch `expansion`: same bytes, new label). Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 \"prove which are\n18\t  truly equivalent, expose the variant that changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network\n19\t  evidence, find the indicator on only one side\") have never been asked -- yet; rows 66 and 68 prepare for it. D17 is the\n20\t  first prompt naming a SECOND evidence type (network) that was not shipped: the likeliest next twist is that it ships.\n21\t- Family names may contain `_` (D14 `polyglot-msbuild_xml`); host profiles seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed,\n22\t  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack (D17: no host file). D14 picked a Windows LOLBin (MSBuild), D10 a WMI\n23\t  host (MOF), D13 a macOS host: the organizers alternate \"language\" days and \"trusted-host abuse\" days. D15-D16\n24\t  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts), D17 back to a Windows automation language (AutoHotkey, sibling of D12 AutoIt).\n25\t  Languages still unpolyglotted: PowerShell v=3, VBA, Tcl, Go, Groovy/Kotlin, R, C#/F# scripts, CI YAML, Makefile/Docker.\n26\t- ~14 drops left (D18-D31).\n27\t  Paths below: `$R=/home/testpwn/huntress-2026`; `source bin/env.sh` puts `bin/` on PATH\n28\t  (pwsh 7.6.6, box-js, js-beautify, webcrack, pycdc/pycdas, 7z, autoit-ripper, ilspycmd). `R/.venv/bin` holds oletools,\n29\t  msoffcrypto-tool, decompyle3/uncompyle6/xdis, pyinstxtractor-ng, LnkParse3, chepy, lxml, and **binary refinery 0.11.1**\n30\t  (AST deobfuscators `ps1` `js` `vba`, batch emulator `bat`, `wshenc`, `xlmdeobf`, `xtone`, `xtchm`, `lnk`, `xtpyi`,\n31\t  `pyc`, `a3x`, `xtnode`, `decompress`, `b64`, `xor`, `rot`...). Usage: `.venv/bin/<unit> < file`.\n32\t\n33\t## 1. Concept table\n34\t\n35\tLegend: INSTALLED = verified with `which`/`.venv/bin` on 2026-10-15; MISSING = not on the box. Never execute a\n36\tfixture's behaviour: run only decoders / AST deobfuscators / emulators on extracted literals.\n37\t\n38\t| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool / approach + exact command | D18+ likelihood |\n39\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n40\t| 1 | PowerShell `.ps1` (v=1 JSON descriptor, `$nativeTypes`) | seen D1 | `$encodedMaterial=[Convert]::FromBase64String(..)`, `function artifact_<hex>`, `[pscustomobject]@{..}` | `base64 -d`; `.venv/bin/ps1 < f.ps1` (INSTALLED, AST deob); `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -c '<decode expr only>'` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n41\t| 2 | JScript WSH `.js` | seen D2 | `ActiveXObject`, `WScript.`, `decode_*/recover_*/inspect_*`, `\"52:90:..\"` | `node $R/hctf/js_sandbox.js f.js`; `box-js --no-kill f.js` (INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/js < f.js` | carried daily |\n42\t| 3 | Batch `.bat/.cmd` + expansion (%/!/call/for) | seen D3 | `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:`, `setlocal EnableDelayedExpansion`, `call set %%..%%` | Python cmd-expansion emulation (solver `batchplan.py`); `.venv/bin/bat < f.bat` (INSTALLED, refinery emulator prints command lines) | carried daily |\n43\t| 4 | VBScript `.vbs` | seen D4 | `Const Codec_<id>`, `Chr(`, `On Error Resume Next`, `Select Case` | lib.codec from the Codec const; `.venv/bin/vba < f.vbs` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n44\t| 5 | Python carriers (pyinstaller/pyarmor/py2exe/cx_Freeze/zipapp/wheel/pyc38) | seen D5 (recovered `.py`), D6 TT real cx_Freeze binary | `*-recovered.py`, `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>`; binary: `MEI\\x0c\\x0b\\x0a\\x0b\\x0e`, `PYZ`, `library.zip` | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)`; `pyinstxtractor-ng x.exe`; `pycdc f.pyc` / `decompyle3 f.pyc` (all INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/xtpyi -l < x.exe` | med: a real frozen binary variant |\n45\t| 6 | Bash `.sh` + bash-advanced (`Feature_<id>`) | seen D6/D7-D16 (D16 ansi_c_quoting, regex_conditional) | `readonly Material_`, `${!ptr}`, `local -A`, `trap`, here-strings | lib.codec; never run bash; `bash -n f.sh` (syntax only) | carried; +2 fixtures some days |\n46\t| 7 | Node ESM `.mjs` | seen D7 | `import`, top-level `await`, `process.env.HUNTRESS_INSPECT_ONLY`, `Buffer.from` | lib.codec static; `webcrack f.mjs -o out/` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n47\t| 8 | PHP polyglot + webshell host | seen D8 | `<?php`, `$descriptor_<id>`, `eval(`/`assert(`, `$_POST`/