 tls.handshake.extensions_server_name` (INSTALLED) and pass the text; `lib.codec.download_graph(plans)` + `download_graph_answer` for chain/root/leaf/unique/count questions | **high**: D17 prompt said it outright |\n107\t| 66 | Semantic equivalence / sibling-outlier questions (\"which variants are equivalent\", \"which one changed the plot\") | gap (prompts D8, D15, D16; never asked) | prompt words equivalent/siblings/odd one out; enum of member names; questions without a per-file artifact | canonicalise every decoded plan (drop campaign/url/path/ids, keep role/steps/adapter/attack/stage_profile/next_language), group by canonical tuple, answer the singleton; `lib.codec.plan_canonical` (built D16 night) | **high**: D16 prompt said it outright |\n108\t| 69 | Download cradles / LOLBin fetch call-sites read from CODE (declared side when code and plan differ) | gap (D17 prompt \"the source code says where it would fetch from\") | `iwr`/`irm`/`Net.WebClient`.`DownloadString`/`Start-BitsTransfer`, `certutil -urlcache -f`, `bitsadmin /transfer`, `mshta http`, `regsvr32 /i:http`, `XMLHTTP.open`, `fetch(`/`http.get(`, `urlopen(`, `Net::HTTP`, `LWP`, `InetGet`, AHK `Download(` | URLs rebuilt from concat/format/char-code literals statically (`.venv/bin/ps1`/`js` fold them); gaps `source-fetch-sites`, `lolbin-download-attack-table` | **high**: next step of the D17 narrative |\n109\t\n110\tCounts: 69 rows; seen 24 (rows 1-18, 48-52, 67), gap 45.\n111\t\n112\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n113\t```\n114\tFINGERPRINT (first 512 bytes + `file`), never by extension:\n115\t FF FE / FE FF / NUL every 2nd byte -> UTF-16: iconv -f UTF-16LE -t UTF-8 first (.reg, PS \"Unicode\" saves, .inf)\n116\t 1F 8B gzip | PK\\x03\\x04 zip/ooxml(.docm .xlsm) | D0 CF 11 E0 OLE(.doc .xls .msi) | ITSF chm | 4C 00 00 00 01 14 02 00 lnk\n117\t E4 52 5C 7B onenote | \\x1bLua luac | FasdUAS compiled AppleScript | MEI\\x0c / PYZ pyinstaller | 0x0d0d0a.. pyc magic\n118\t #@~^ ..^#~@ = Script-Encoder (.vbe/.jse) -> .venv/bin/wshenc < f\n119\tSHEBANG/HEADER -> language:\n120\t #!..perl / use strict; / my $descriptor_ -> perl (D15)   DESCRIPTOR_<HEX> = / def build_plan_ / ->(_env) -> ruby (D16)\n121\t #Requires AutoHotkey / x := \"..\" / Map( / ; comments -> autohotkey v2 (D17; family polyglot-auto_hotkey, underscore)\n122\t #!..tclsh / set x \"v\" / proc -> tcl  x <- v / library( -> R          package main / := -> go\n123\t fn main / let mut / r#\"..\"# -> rust  val/fun + plugins{ -> kotlin(.kts)   pipeline{ stages{ / def x= -> groovy/Jenkinsfile\n124\t BEGIN{ / getline -> awk              target:\\n\\tcmd / $(shell -> make     FROM / RUN -> Dockerfile\n125\t on:/jobs:/runs-on: -> GH Actions     stages:/script: -> GitLab CI          - hosts:/tasks: -> ansible\n126\t resource \"x\" / provisioner \"local-exec\" -> terraform    Windows Registry Editor 5.00 -> .reg\n127\t [Version] Signature=\"$CHICAGO$\" -> .inf   [InternetShortcut] -> .url   [Shell] Command= -> .scf\n128\t <xsl:stylesheet + msxsl:script -> XSLT (msxsl/wmic)   <scriptlet> -> SCT   <job> -> WSF   <hta:application> -> HTA\n129\t <Project ..msbuild> + UsingTask -> MSBuild    Installer + [RunInstaller(true)] -> InstallUtil C#\n130\t Sub AutoOpen/Document_Open/Attribute VB_Name -> VBA   =EXEC(/=FORMULA( in a sheet -> XLM\n131\t instance of __EventFilter -> MOF        #r \"nuget: -> csx   let/printfn/|> -> fsx   Deno./Bun. -> deno/bun\n132\tPLAN FIRST (the lane's contract since D2):\n133\t grep raw AND utf-16-decoded text for HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+ / Codec_ / CODEC_ / HUNTRESS-CODEC / MATERIAL_ / descriptor\n134\t descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n135\t   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const, seen D16) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n136\t material may wrap across lines (`|` YAML block, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\` continuation, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat):\n137\t   join the literal pieces, strip whitespace/separators, THEN peel\n138\t peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n139\t   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n140\t   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n141\t copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code\n142\tLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n143\t PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n144\t JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n145\t VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n146\t Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n147\t XLM          .venv/bin/xlmdeobf < f.xls      OneNote .venv/bin/xtone -l < f.one     CHM .venv/bin/xtchm -l < f.chm\n148\t LNK          .venv/bin/lnk < f.lnk           AutoIt  autoit-ripper x.exe out/ | .venv/bin/a3x < f\n149\t Python       swap exec/eval->print, run with python3 -I in an empty dir; marshal blob -> pycdc / xdis (match version)\n150\t compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n151\t PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\n152\tNEVER: run the fixture's interpreter on the file (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/Rscript/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File);\n153\t `perl -MO=Deparse` and `make -n` still execute BEGIN/$(shell) -> strip first; apply XSLT; open URLs from the plan.\n154\tSYNTHETIC LABELS (if a new language brings code-shape questions): read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`,\n155\t `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch `expansion` = STATEMENT-ONLY table by default (D15 run_for_time:false pools,\n156\t every contract from D16 incl. the single); if a carried label is rejected on unchanged bytes, the GM regime moved:\n157\t tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh before probing synonyms.\n158\tEQUIVALENCE/OUTLIER prompt (D16 \"same logic, which changed the plot\"): only answer it if a question asks; then compare\n159\t canonical plans (role, steps, adapter, attack, stage_profile, next_language), never campaign/url/ids which always differ.\n160\tNETWORK-RECONCILE prompt (D17 \"source vs network evidence, indicator on one side\"): flavour unless a question/net file exists;\n161\t then lib.codec.reconcile({member: plan}, har/zeek/text) -> reconcile_answer(r, kind, accepted, what=); pcap: tshark fields\n162\t to text first. Graph/chain/root/leaf/count ids: lib.codec.download_graph(plans) -> download_graph_answer. Unknown plan-key\n163\t suffix (-verdict, -language): lib.codec.plan_answer(id, plan, q).\n164\tATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n165\t .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 plans so far used parent T1059.\n166\t```\n167\t\n168\t## Readiness gaps\n169\tBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16 night source-encoding-normalize, equivalence-outlier-compare, batch-expansion-regime-lib, v3-next-lang-fixture-battery, wsh-script-encoder-decode, ruby-perl-pack-reps, yaml-ci-host-route, reg-inf-host-route; D17 night download-graph-model, network-evidence-reconcile, plan-key-passthrough, indicator-refang-normalize, ahk-compiled-exe-extract, vba-module-route, dockerfile-makefile-route (all `lib.codec`). Given up: python-exec-onion-static (2 attempts, `import ast` banned -> replaced by python-onion-regex-fold). Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (no csv/ast/tokenize/shlex/marshal; dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile OK). Resolved: mastery-runner-budget (D17 5-set Mastery 12.7 s).\n170\t\n171\t```json\n172\t[\n173\t  {\"id\": \"network-evidence-indicators\", \"concept\": \"extract fetch indicators from network evidence (pcap/pcapng, HAR, Zeek/proxy/DNS logs, Sysmon EID 3/22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"RETRY (1st attempt D17 night reverted: `import csv` is outside the prebuild gate's allowlist -- hand-split TSV/CSV with re/str.split, quotes via a small regex). D17 prompt: 'the generated network evidence says where the requests actually went'. network_indicators(data, name='')->[{kind: http|dns|tls|conn, host, url, ip, port, method, user_agent, src}] sniffing by magic/shape: pcap D4C3B2A1/A1B2C3D4 and pcapng 0A0D0D0A via dpkt (allowed) or struct -- HTTP request line + Host, DNS qname (+A/CNAME answers), TLS ClientHello SNI, TCP SYN dst ip:port; feed the list straight into lib.codec.observed_fetches()/reconcile(). tshark (INSTALLED) is the test oracle only. Fixtures: synthetic pcap/pcapng built with struct from today's decoded plan urls, one url added and one removed.\"},\n174\t  {\"id\": \"source-fetch-sites\", \"concept\": \"declared fetch targets read from the CODE (download cradles), not only the plan\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 prompt: 'the source code says where it would fetch from'. If a fixture's code and plan disagree (or a member has no plan url), the declared side must come from call sites. fetch_sites(src, name='')->[{api, url, method, line}] for PS Invoke-WebRequest/iwr/irm/Net.WebClient.DownloadString|DownloadFile|UploadString/Start-BitsTransfer, certutil -urlcache -split -f, bitsadmin /transfer, curl/wget/Invoke-RestMethod, mshta http.., regsvr32 /i:http, JS/VBS/VBA MSXML2.XMLHTTP|ServerXMLHTTP|WinHttp .open, Node fetch/http(s).get/axios, Python urllib.request.urlopen/requests.get|post, Ruby Net::HTTP/URI.open, Perl LWP get/HTTP::Tiny, PHP file_get_contents/curl_init, Lua socket.http/ngx.location.capture, AHK Download()/WinHttpRequest, AutoIt InetGet/InetRead, AppleScript do shell script \\\"curl. Rebuild URLs from '+'/'&'/'.'/'..' concat, -f format, join() and char-code arrays over the file's own literals (re only; no ast/eval). Gate: on the D17 bundle every v=1/v=2/v=3 member's fetch_sites url equals (or is absent from) its plan url.\"},\n175\t  {\"id\": \"reconcile-indicator-kinds\", \"concept\": \"one-sided indicators that are not URLs (IP, user agent, file name, port, JA3)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib.codec.reconcile compares urls/hosts only. Extend the report with ips (conn dst / DNS A answers), user_agents (HAR request headers, Zeek http user_agent, PS sample UA indicator), file_names (URI basename, Content-Disposition, plan file_path/next_stage basename), ports; same {declared_only, observed_only, both} shape and reconcile_answer(what='user_agents.observed_only' ...). The question 'which indicator shows up on only one side' may name any indicator kind the lane already extracts (url, wallet, mutex, UA, file).\"},\n176\t  {\"id\": \"http-redirect-dns-resolve\", \"concept\": \"follow redirects / DNS CNAME+A so declared and observed sides join\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Where the requests actually went' can differ by a 30x Location hop or a CNAME. From HAR (response.redirectURL / Location header / status), pcap HTTP responses and DNS answers build host->ip and url->final_url maps; reconcile() should count a declared url as fetched when its redirect chain or resolved IP appears, and report the redirect target as the observed-only value. Expose resolve_chain(observed)->{url: [hops]}.\"},\n177\t  {\"id\": \"pcap-http-object-hashes\", \"concept\": \"reassemble HTTP bodies from pcap -> name/size/sha256/next-stage decode\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Depends on network-evidence-indicators. dpkt TCP reassembly by (flow, seq) for port-80 / plain HTTP, Content-Length and chunked transfer-encoding, gzip Content-Encoding -> [{uri, status, content_type, size, sha256, body}]. Bodies that are scripts go back through find_codecs / the V3 marker peel (the fetched next stage). Questions likely: sha256 of the downloaded payload, its file name, its decoded plan values.\"},\n178\t  {\"id\": \"sysmon-proxy-log-fetches\", \"concept\": \"observed network side from Sysmon / proxy / web-server logs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"observed_fetches() covers HAR, Zeek TSV and free text. Add: Sysmon EID 3 (DestinationHostname/DestinationIp/Port, Image) and EID 22 (QueryName, QueryResults, Image) from EVTX (Evtx lib allowed) or exported XML/JSON; IIS/W3C `#Fields:` logs; Apache/nginx combined; squid native access.log (`ts elapsed client code/status bytes METHOD URL`). Keep the Image/process so an 'only one side' answer can name the process that fetched. No csv module (gate): split by regex.\"},\n179\t  {\"id\": \"ps-v3-polyglot-route\", \"concept\": \"PowerShell as a v=3 polyglot (.ps1/.psm1/.psd1/.ps1xml)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PS is the only D1 language with no v=3 fixture; a polyglot-powershell day would put the marker in `<# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:.. #>` block comments or `#` lines and the descriptor in `$descriptor_x = '..'`, `[string]$descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\"`, here-strings `@' .. '@` / `@\\\" .. \\\"@`, or a `.psd1` hashtable `Descriptor = '..'`. Ensure the lib marker/descriptor helpers accept all of these and that an is_v3(src) check exists so callers route v=3 before the v=1 `$encodedMaterial`/`$nativeTypes` JSON path. Fixture battery: carried D17 polyglot plans re-wrapped in each PS form.\"},\n180\t  {\"id\": \"lolbin-download-attack-table\", \"concept\": \"fetch API / LOLBin -> ATT&CK + adapter label table\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Data table in lib.scripts used by source-fetch-sites: certutil T1105 (+T1140 when -decode), bitsadmin/Start-BitsTransfer T1197, mshta T1218.005, regsvr32 /i T1218.010, rundll32 T1218.011, msiexec /i http T1218.007, curl/wget/IWR/WebClient/XMLHTTP/fetch T1105, upload verbs T1041/T1567. Remember the lane's GM history: plans' attack= wins; this table only fills ids with no plan value, return candidates in order.\"},\n181\t  {\"id\": \"python-onion-regex-fold\", \"concept\": \"Python exec onions folded without ast/marshal\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Replaces python-exec-onion-static (given up after 2 attempts: `import ast` is outside the gate allowlist). Regex-fold literal call chains innermost-first with base64/zlib/codecs/binascii only: b64decode/b32decode/b85decode, zlib.decompress, bytes.fromhex, codecs.decode(..,'rot13'), [::-1], .decode(); stop at exec/eval/marshal.loads and return the last literal. marshal blobs: report only (xdis not in the allowlist).\"},\n182\t  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n183\t  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n184\t  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n185\t  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n186\t  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n187\t  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n188\t  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n189\t  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n190\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script  (only to parse; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild payloads).\"},\n191\t  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk (and future .tcl .r .groovy .kts .go .rs .awk .yml .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n192\t  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n193\t  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..).\"}\n194\t]\n195\t```\n196\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"114a275e-f12e-4e0c-98b2-ce73e35ca9d8","uuid":"fe0b96e4-6dfe-4376-a822-bf39278702b7","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:02:02.675Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/114a275e-f12e-4e0c-98b2-ce73e35ca9d8/tool-results/b8wlphbeq.txt","content":"# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D17 seen vs. D18+ candidates)\n\nUpdated 2026-10-17 after D17 (1139 ids, 127 members; D17 added AutoHotkey `.ahk`, all modes first try, single T+13 s); gaps\nre-queued 2026-10-18 after the D17-night prebuild (7 built, 1 given up, 1 pending retry). Read with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\nactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\nhave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n\nContext that drives the likelihood column:\n- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n  The carried solver (`challenges/day17/scripting-fetch-quest/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n  `analyse_v3`; ran unchanged D9-D17) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, on one line, peelable by hex/base64/\n  reverse within 3 layers. The real D18+ risk is not a new language — it is a new **carrier/encoding/container**, a\n  new **synthetic-label family** (D2-D7 era), or a **GM label-regime flip** on an old one (D15 pool-keyed, D16 date-keyed\n  batch `expansion`: same bytes, new label). Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 \"prove which are\n  truly equivalent, expose the variant that changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network\n  evidence, find the indicator on only one side\") have never been asked -- yet; rows 66 and 68 prepare for it. D17 is the\n  first prompt naming a SECOND evidence type (network) that was not shipped: the likeliest next twist is that it ships.\n- Family names may contain `_` (D14 `polyglot-msbuild_xml`); host profiles seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed,\n  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack (D17: no host file). D14 picked a Windows LOLBin (MSBuild), D10 a WMI\n  host (MOF), D13 a macOS host: the organizers alternate \"language\" days and \"trusted-host abuse\" days. D15-D16\n  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts), D17 back to a Windows automation language (AutoHotkey, sibling of D12 AutoIt).\n  Languages still unpolyglotted: PowerShell v=3, VBA, Tcl, Go, Groovy/Kotlin, R, C#/F# scripts, CI YAML, Makefile/Docker.\n- ~14 drops left (D18-D31).\n  Paths below: `$R=/home/testpwn/huntress-2026`; `source bin/env.sh` puts `bin/` on PATH\n  (pwsh 7.6.6, box-js, js-beautify, webcrack, pycdc/pycdas, 7z, autoit-ripper, ilspycmd). `R/.venv/bin` holds oletools,\n  msoffcrypto-tool, decompyle3/uncompyle6/xdis, pyinstxtractor-ng, LnkParse3, chepy, lxml, and **binary refinery 0.11.1**\n  (AST deobfuscators `ps1` `js` `vba`, batch emulator `bat`, `wshenc`, `xlmdeobf`, `xtone`, `xtchm`, `lnk`, `xtpyi`,\n  `pyc`, `a3x`, `xtnode`, `decompress`, `b64`, `xor`, `rot`...). Usage: `.venv/bin/<unit> < file`.\n\n## 1. Concept table\n\nLegend: INSTALLED = verified with `which`/`.venv/bin` on 2026-10-15; MISSING = not on the box. Never execute a\nfixture's behaviour: run only decoders / AST deobfuscators / emulators on extracted literals.\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool / approach + exact command | D18+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | PowerShell `.ps1` (v=1 JSON descriptor, `$nativeTypes`) | seen D1 | `$encodedMaterial=[Convert]::FromBase64String(..)`, `function artifact_<hex>`, `[pscustomobject]@{..}` | `base64 -d`; `.venv/bin/ps1 < f.ps1` (INSTALLED, AST deob); `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -c '<decode expr only>'` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 2 | JScript WSH `.js` | seen D2 | `ActiveXObject`, `WScript.`, `decode_*/recover_*/inspect_*`, `\"52:90:..\"` | `node $R/hctf/js_sandbox.js f.js`; `box-js --no-kill f.js` (INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/js < f.js` | carried daily |\n| 3 | Batch `.bat/.cmd` + expansion (%/!/call/for) | seen D3 | `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:`, `setlocal EnableDelayedExpansion`, `call set %%..%%` | Python cmd-expansion emulation (solver `batchplan.py`); `.venv/bin/bat < f.bat` (INSTALLED, refinery emulator prints command lines) | carried daily |\n| 4 | VBScript `.vbs` | seen D4 | `Const Codec_<id>`, `Chr(`, `On Error Resume Next`, `Select Case` | lib.codec from the Codec const; `.venv/bin/vba < f.vbs` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 5 | Python carriers (pyinstaller/pyarmor/py2exe/cx_Freeze/zipapp/wheel/pyc38) | seen D5 (recovered `.py`), D6 TT real cx_Freeze binary | `*-recovered.py`, `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>`; binary: `MEI\\x0c\\x0b\\x0a\\x0b\\x0e`, `PYZ`, `library.zip` | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)`; `pyinstxtractor-ng x.exe`; `pycdc f.pyc` / `decompyle3 f.pyc` (all INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/xtpyi -l < x.exe` | med: a real frozen binary variant |\n| 6 | Bash `.sh` + bash-advanced (`Feature_<id>`) | seen D6/D7-D16 (D16 ansi_c_quoting, regex_conditional) | `readonly Material_`, `${!ptr}`, `local -A`, `trap`, here-strings | lib.codec; never run bash; `bash -n f.sh` (syntax only) | carried; +2 fixtures some days |\n| 7 | Node ESM `.mjs` | seen D7 | `import`, top-level `await`, `process.env.HUNTRESS_INSPECT_ONLY`, `Buffer.from` | lib.codec static; `webcrack f.mjs -o out/` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 8 | PHP polyglot + webshell host | seen D8 | `<?php`, `$descriptor_<id>`, `eval(`/`assert(`, `$_POST`/`$_REQUEST` | V3_MARK peel; `php` MISSING (`apt install php-cli` for `php -l`/token dump only) | carried daily |\n| 9 | WSF / HTA hosts | seen D8 | `<job><script language=..>`, `<hta:application>`, mixed JScript+VBS | extract each `<script>` body (lxml/bs4 INSTALLED) and route by language | carried |\n| 10 | Lua + OpenResty host | seen D9 | `local descriptor_`, `--` comments, `ngx.`, `inert_handler_<id>` | V3_MARK; `lua`/`luac` MISSING (`apt install lua5.4`) | carried |\n| 11 | SCT scriptlet (regsvr32 /i:url scrobj.dll, Squiblydoo) | seen D9 (host) | `<?xml?><scriptlet><registration progid=..>`, `<![CDATA[` | strip CDATA -> JScript/VBS route | carried |\n| 12 | WMI MOF | seen D10 | `#pragma namespace`, `instance of __EventFilter`, `ActiveScriptEventConsumer`, `ScriptText =` | V3_MARK; ScriptText is a C-escaped JS/VBS string -> unescape then route | carried |\n| 13 | TypeScript | seen D11 | type annotations, `interface`, `as const`, `.ts` | V3_MARK; no tsc needed (strip types or read literals) | carried |\n| 14 | AutoIt `.au3` | seen D12 | `Global Const $descriptor_`, `;` comments, `#include <..>`, `Execute(`, `BinaryToString` | V3_MARK; compiled: `autoit-ripper x.exe out/` / `.venv/bin/a3x < x.a3x` (INSTALLED) | carried; compiled a3x = med |\n| 15 | AppleScript (source) | seen D13 | `property descriptor_<id> :`, `--` comments, `do shell script`, `osascript -e` | V3_MARK; compiled `.scpt` (`FasdUAS` magic) = no decompiler (MISSING: applescript-disassembler) | carried; `.scpt` = low/med |\n| 16 | MSBuild `.proj` inline task | seen D14 | `<Project xmlns=..msbuild..>`, `<UsingTask TaskFactory=\"CodeTaskFactory\">`, `<Code Type=\"Fragment\">` C# CDATA, `<HuntressDescriptor>` | V3_MARK in `<!-- -->`; lxml for the property element | carried |\n| 17 | Perl `.pl` + perl_cgi host | seen D15 | `#!/usr/bin/env perl`, `use strict;`, `my $descriptor_`, `print \"Content-Type:` | V3_MARK; `perl -MO=Deparse f.pl` (INSTALLED, parse-only, BEGIN blocks still run - strip them) | carried |\n| 18 | Ruby `.rb` (+ Rack host) | seen D16 | `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` + `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` (uppercase const), `require`, `def ..end`, `def build_plan_<id>` returning `{ descriptor: DESCRIPTOR_<ID> }`, host `ruby_rack` = `INERT_RACK_<ID> = ->(_env) { [200, {..}, [..]] }` lambda | V3_MARK (carried solver, unchanged); `ruby -c f.rb` syntax only; ERB/Rails `<%= %>` hosts still unseen | carried |\n| 67 | AutoHotkey `.ahk` (v2) | seen D17 | `#Requires AutoHotkey v2.0`, `; HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..`, `descriptor_<8hex> := \"..\"`, `buildPlan_<id>() { global ..; return Map(\"descriptor\", ..) }`; v1 legacy would be `x = text` unquoted + `%x%` derefs + `( .. )` continuation sections | V3_MARK (carried solver, unchanged); compiled Ahk2Exe PE = RT_RCDATA `>AUTOHOTKEY SCRIPT<` -> lib.codec carrier walk (built D17 night, also AHK v1 `x = text` / continuation sections) | carried; compiled exe / v1 syntax = low/med |\n| 19 | PowerShell module / `.psm1` `.psd1` `.ps1xml` (v=3 polyglot-powershell) | gap (PS only v=1) | `Export-ModuleMember`, `FunctionsToExport`, `<Types><Type><ScriptMethod><Script>`, `<#  #>` block comments (marker may sit inside `<# #>`) | `.venv/bin/ps1 < f.psm1`; lxml for ps1xml `<Script>` nodes | **high**: PS is the canonical malware language and has no v=3 fixture |\n| 20 | Tcl / Expect | gap | `#!/usr/bin/tclsh`, `set descriptor_x \"...\"` (no `=`!), `proc`, `puts`, `binary decode base64`, `{braces}` strings | `tclsh` MISSING (`apt install tcl`); static: regex `set\\s+descriptor_\\w+\\s+[\"{]` | med |\n| 21 | R script | gap | `<-` assignment, `library(`, `base64enc::`, `rawToChar(`, `system(`, `#` comments | `Rscript` MISSING (`apt install r-base-core`, big); static `<-` descriptor regex | low/med |\n| 22 | Groovy / Jenkinsfile | gap | `pipeline { agent .. stages`, `sh '''..'''`, `def x = \"..\"`, `\"cmd\".execute()`, `.decodeBase64()` | `groovy` MISSING (java INSTALLED; jar from apache); static read | med: CI-abuse host fits \"trusted toolchain\" theme |\n| 23 | Kotlin script `.kts` / Gradle `build.gradle.kts` | gap | `val descriptor_x = \"..\"`, `plugins {`, `tasks.register`, `Runtime.getRuntime().exec`, `Base64.getDecoder()` | `kotlinc` MISSING; static | med (Gradle build abuse) |\n| 24 | Go (`go run`, `//go:generate`) | gap | `package main`, `descriptor_x := \"..\"` (`:=` breaks current regex), `exec.Command`, raw `` `..` `` strings | `go vet f.go` (INSTALLED /usr/bin/go; never `go run`) | med |\n| 25 | Rust script / `build.rs` | gap | `fn main()`, `const DESCRIPTOR_X: &str = \"..\"`, `std::process::Command`, `r#\"..\"#` raw strings, `\\u{..}` | `rustc` INSTALLED (don't build); static | low/med (`build.rs` = build-time abuse) |\n| 26 | AWK program | gap | `BEGIN {`, `system(`, `\"cmd\" \\| getline`, `#!/usr/bin/awk -f` | `gawk --lint -f f.awk /dev/null` is NOT safe (BEGIN runs) -> static only | med (LOLBin `awk`, GTFOBins) |\n| 27 | sed script | gap | `#!/bin/sed -f`, `s/../../e` (GNU exec flag), `w /path` | static | low |\n| 28 | Makefile | gap | `target: deps` + TAB recipes, `$(shell ..)`, `DESCRIPTOR := ..` (`:=`), `.PHONY` | lib.codec Makefile route (built D17 night: `\\` joins, `DESCRIPTOR_X := ..`, `#` marker); never `make -n` (evaluates `$(shell)`) | med (build-system abuse theme) |\n| 29 | Dockerfile | gap | `FROM`, `RUN curl .. \\| sh`, `ENV`, `ARG`, `# HUNTRESS..` comments, `COPY --chmod` | lib.codec Dockerfile route (built D17 night: `ARG/ENV DESCRIPTOR_X=`, `RUN echo .. \\| base64 -d`); never `docker build` | med |\n| 30 | CI YAML (GitHub Actions / GitLab CI) | gap | `on: [push]`, `jobs:`, `runs-on:`, `steps: - run:` + block scalar, `stages:`, `script:`; block scalars span lines | `.venv/bin/python -c 'import yaml,sys;print(yaml.safe_load(open(sys.argv[1])))' f.yml` (INSTALLED); `yq` MISSING | med/high: supply-chain host, family would be `polyglot-github_actions`-style |\n| 31 | Ansible playbook | gap | `- hosts:`, `tasks:`, `ansible.builtin.shell:`, `become: true`, `vars:` | yaml.safe_load (INSTALLED); ansible MISSING (not needed) | low/med |\n| 32 | Terraform HCL | gap | `resource \"null_resource\"`, `provisioner \"local-exec\" { command = ..}`, `data \"external\"`, `locals {` | `terraform fmt -check` (INSTALLED; never init/plan); python-hcl2 MISSING | low/med |\n| 33 | XSL/XSLT via `msxsl.exe` / `wmic /format:` (Squiblytwo) | gap | `<xsl:stylesheet`, `xmlns:msxsl=\"urn:schemas-microsoft-com:xslt\"`, `<msxsl:script language=\"JScript\" implements-prefix=..>` CDATA | lxml parse (INSTALLED), pull `msxsl:script` text -> JS/VBS route; NEVER apply the transform; `xsltproc` MISSING | **high**: Windows trusted-host abuse, sibling of D9 SCT / D14 MSBuild |\n| 34 | InstallUtil (.NET `[RunInstaller(true)]` C#) | gap | `System.Configuration.Install.Installer`, `Uninstall(IDictionary)` override, `/U` | read C#; compiled: `ilspycmd x.dll` (INSTALLED) | med (LOLBin family with MSBuild) |\n| 35 | C# script `.csx` (csi / dotnet-script) | gap | `#r \"nuget:..`, top-level statements, `#load` | static; `dotnet` INSTALLED, `csi`/`dotnet-script` MISSING | med |\n| 36 | F# script `.fsx` | gap | `#r`, `let descriptor_x = \"..\"`, `printfn`, `\\|>` | static (`dotnet fsi` would execute) | low |\n| 37 | rundll32 `javascript:` / mshtml RunHTMLApplication one-liner | gap | `rundll32.exe javascript:\"\\..\\mshtml,RunHTMLApplication \";..` | treat tail as JScript -> `node $R/hctf/js_sandbox.js` | med (inside a .lnk/.bat host) |\n| 38 | CHM (compiled HTML help) | gap | `ITSF` magic, `.chm`, `hh.exe`, HTML with `<OBJECT classid=..ADB880A6..>` shortcut command | `.venv/bin/xtchm -l < f.chm` (INSTALLED); `7z x f.chm -oout` (INSTALLED) | med (container carrier) |\n| 39 | LNK with embedded command line | gap | `4C 00 00 00 01 14 02 00` magic, args `/c powershell -enc ..`, padded whitespace args | `.venv/bin/lnk < f.lnk` / `lnkparse f.lnk` (INSTALLED) | med |\n| 40 | VBA macros (`.bas`, `.docm/.xlsm`, OLE `.doc`) | gap | `Sub AutoOpen()`, `Document_Open`, `Attribute VB_Name`, `Shell`, `CreateObject(\"WScript.Shell\")`, `vbaProject.bin` | lib.codec carrier walk decompresses MS-OVBA module source from vbaProject.bin (built D17 night) then Codec_/marker scan; `.venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f.docm` oracle; `.venv/bin/vba < module.bas`; `pcodedmp`/`vbapc` for VBA stomping (all INSTALLED); `msoffcrypto-tool -p VelvetSweatshop` | **high**: classic, and the 4th WSH-family language not yet polyglotted |\n| 41 | Excel 4.0 / XLM macros | gap | `Macro1` sheet, `=EXEC(`, `=CALL(`, `=FORMULA(`, `CHAR(` chains, hidden/very-hidden sheets, BOUNDSHEET | `.venv/bin/xlmdeobf < f.xls` (INSTALLED, refinery port); standalone `xlmdeobfuscator` MISSING (`pip install XLMMacroDeobfuscator`) | med |\n| 42 | OneNote `.one` embedded scripts | gap | GUID `E4525C7B-8CD8-A74D-AEB1-5378D0