uild    Installer + [RunInstaller(true)] -> InstallUtil C#\n Sub AutoOpen/Document_Open/Attribute VB_Name -> VBA   =EXEC(/=FORMULA( in a sheet -> XLM\n instance of __EventFilter -> MOF        #r \"nuget: -> csx   let/printfn/|> -> fsx   Deno./Bun. -> deno/bun\nPLAN FIRST (the lane's contract since D2):\n grep raw AND utf-16-decoded text for HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+ / Codec_ / CODEC_ / HUNTRESS-CODEC / MATERIAL_ / descriptor\n descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const, seen D16) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n material may wrap across lines (`|` YAML block, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\` continuation, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat):\n   join the literal pieces, strip whitespace/separators, THEN peel\n peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code\nLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n XLM          .venv/bin/xlmdeobf < f.xls      OneNote .venv/bin/xtone -l < f.one     CHM .venv/bin/xtchm -l < f.chm\n LNK          .venv/bin/lnk < f.lnk           AutoIt  autoit-ripper x.exe out/ | .venv/bin/a3x < f\n Python       swap exec/eval->print, run with python3 -I in an empty dir; marshal blob -> pycdc / xdis (match version)\n compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\nNEVER: run the fixture's interpreter on the file (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/Rscript/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File);\n `perl -MO=Deparse` and `make -n` still execute BEGIN/$(shell) -> strip first; apply XSLT; open URLs from the plan.\nSYNTHETIC LABELS (if a new language brings code-shape questions): read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`,\n `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch `expansion` = STATEMENT-ONLY table by default (D15 run_for_time:false pools,\n every contract from D16 incl. the single); if a carried label is rejected on unchanged bytes, the GM regime moved:\n tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh before probing synonyms.\nEQUIVALENCE/OUTLIER prompt (D16 \"same logic, which changed the plot\"): only answer it if a question asks; then compare\n canonical plans (role, steps, adapter, attack, stage_profile, next_language), never campaign/url/ids which always differ.\nNETWORK-RECONCILE prompt (D17 \"source vs network evidence, indicator on one side\"): flavour unless a question/net file exists;\n then lib.codec.reconcile({member: plan}, har/zeek/text) -> reconcile_answer(r, kind, accepted, what=); pcap: tshark fields\n to text first. Graph/chain/root/leaf/count ids: lib.codec.download_graph(plans) -> download_graph_answer. Unknown plan-key\n suffix (-verdict, -language): lib.codec.plan_answer(id, plan, q).\nATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 plans so far used parent T1059.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16 night source-encoding-normalize, equivalence-outlier-compare, batch-expansion-regime-lib, v3-next-lang-fixture-battery, wsh-script-encoder-decode, ruby-perl-pack-reps, yaml-ci-host-route, reg-inf-host-route; D17 night download-graph-model, network-evidence-reconcile, plan-key-passthrough, indicator-refang-normalize, ahk-compiled-exe-extract, vba-module-route, dockerfile-makefile-route (all `lib.codec`). Given up: python-exec-onion-static (2 attempts, `import ast` banned -> replaced by python-onion-regex-fold). Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (no csv/ast/tokenize/shlex/marshal; dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile OK). Resolved: mastery-runner-budget (D17 5-set Mastery 12.7 s).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"network-evidence-indicators\", \"concept\": \"extract fetch indicators from network evidence (pcap/pcapng, HAR, Zeek/proxy/DNS logs, Sysmon EID 3/22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"RETRY (1st attempt D17 night reverted: `import csv` is outside the prebuild gate's allowlist -- hand-split TSV/CSV with re/str.split, quotes via a small regex). D17 prompt: 'the generated network evidence says where the requests actually went'. network_indicators(data, name='')->[{kind: http|dns|tls|conn, host, url, ip, port, method, user_agent, src}] sniffing by magic/shape: pcap D4C3B2A1/A1B2C3D4 and pcapng 0A0D0D0A via dpkt (allowed) or struct -- HTTP request line + Host, DNS qname (+A/CNAME answers), TLS ClientHello SNI, TCP SYN dst ip:port; feed the list straight into lib.codec.observed_fetches()/reconcile(). tshark (INSTALLED) is the test oracle only. Fixtures: synthetic pcap/pcapng built with struct from today's decoded plan urls, one url added and one removed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"source-fetch-sites\", \"concept\": \"declared fetch targets read from the CODE (download cradles), not only the plan\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 prompt: 'the source code says where it would fetch from'. If a fixture's code and plan disagree (or a member has no plan url), the declared side must come from call sites. fetch_sites(src, name='')->[{api, url, method, line}] for PS Invoke-WebRequest/iwr/irm/Net.WebClient.DownloadString|DownloadFile|UploadString/Start-BitsTransfer, certutil -urlcache -split -f, bitsadmin /transfer, curl/wget/Invoke-RestMethod, mshta http.., regsvr32 /i:http, JS/VBS/VBA MSXML2.XMLHTTP|ServerXMLHTTP|WinHttp .open, Node fetch/http(s).get/axios, Python urllib.request.urlopen/requests.get|post, Ruby Net::HTTP/URI.open, Perl LWP get/HTTP::Tiny, PHP file_get_contents/curl_init, Lua socket.http/ngx.location.capture, AHK Download()/WinHttpRequest, AutoIt InetGet/InetRead, AppleScript do shell script \\\"curl. Rebuild URLs from '+'/'&'/'.'/'..' concat, -f format, join() and char-code arrays over the file's own literals (re only; no ast/eval). Gate: on the D17 bundle every v=1/v=2/v=3 member's fetch_sites url equals (or is absent from) its plan url.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"reconcile-indicator-kinds\", \"concept\": \"one-sided indicators that are not URLs (IP, user agent, file name, port, JA3)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib.codec.reconcile compares urls/hosts only. Extend the report with ips (conn dst / DNS A answers), user_agents (HAR request headers, Zeek http user_agent, PS sample UA indicator), file_names (URI basename, Content-Disposition, plan file_path/next_stage basename), ports; same {declared_only, observed_only, both} shape and reconcile_answer(what='user_agents.observed_only' ...). The question 'which indicator shows up on only one side' may name any indicator kind the lane already extracts (url, wallet, mutex, UA, file).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"http-redirect-dns-resolve\", \"concept\": \"follow redirects / DNS CNAME+A so declared and observed sides join\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Where the requests actually went' can differ by a 30x Location hop or a CNAME. From HAR (response.redirectURL / Location header / status), pcap HTTP responses and DNS answers build host->ip and url->final_url maps; reconcile() should count a declared url as fetched when its redirect chain or resolved IP appears, and report the redirect target as the observed-only value. Expose resolve_chain(observed)->{url: [hops]}.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pcap-http-object-hashes\", \"concept\": \"reassemble HTTP bodies from pcap -> name/size/sha256/next-stage decode\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Depends on network-evidence-indicators. dpkt TCP reassembly by (flow, seq) for port-80 / plain HTTP, Content-Length and chunked transfer-encoding, gzip Content-Encoding -> [{uri, status, content_type, size, sha256, body}]. Bodies that are scripts go back through find_codecs / the V3 marker peel (the fetched next stage). Questions likely: sha256 of the downloaded payload, its file name, its decoded plan values.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sysmon-proxy-log-fetches\", \"concept\": \"observed network side from Sysmon / proxy / web-server logs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"observed_fetches() covers HAR, Zeek TSV and free text. Add: Sysmon EID 3 (DestinationHostname/DestinationIp/Port, Image) and EID 22 (QueryName, QueryResults, Image) from EVTX (Evtx lib allowed) or exported XML/JSON; IIS/W3C `#Fields:` logs; Apache/nginx combined; squid native access.log (`ts elapsed client code/status bytes METHOD URL`). Keep the Image/process so an 'only one side' answer can name the process that fetched. No csv module (gate): split by regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-v3-polyglot-route\", \"concept\": \"PowerShell as a v=3 polyglot (.ps1/.psm1/.psd1/.ps1xml)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PS is the only D1 language with no v=3 fixture; a polyglot-powershell day would put the marker in `<# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:.. #>` block comments or `#` lines and the descriptor in `$descriptor_x = '..'`, `[string]$descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\"`, here-strings `@' .. '@` / `@\\\" .. \\\"@`, or a `.psd1` hashtable `Descriptor = '..'`. Ensure the lib marker/descriptor helpers accept all of these and that an is_v3(src) check exists so callers route v=3 before the v=1 `$encodedMaterial`/`$nativeTypes` JSON path. Fixture battery: carried D17 polyglot plans re-wrapped in each PS form.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lolbin-download-attack-table\", \"concept\": \"fetch API / LOLBin -> ATT&CK + adapter label table\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Data table in lib.scripts used by source-fetch-sites: certutil T1105 (+T1140 when -decode), bitsadmin/Start-BitsTransfer T1197, mshta T1218.005, regsvr32 /i T1218.010, rundll32 T1218.011, msiexec /i http T1218.007, curl/wget/IWR/WebClient/XMLHTTP/fetch T1105, upload verbs T1041/T1567. Remember the lane's GM history: plans' attack= wins; this table only fills ids with no plan value, return candidates in order.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"python-onion-regex-fold\", \"concept\": \"Python exec onions folded without ast/marshal\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Replaces python-exec-onion-static (given up after 2 attempts: `import ast` is outside the gate allowlist). Regex-fold literal call chains innermost-first with base64/zlib/codecs/binascii only: b64decode/b32decode/b85decode, zlib.decompress, bytes.fromhex, codecs.decode(..,'rot13'), [::-1], .decode(); stop at exec/eval/marshal.loads and return the last literal. marshal blobs: report only (xdis not in the allowlist).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script  (only to parse; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild payloads).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk (and future .tcl .r .groovy .kts .go .rs .awk .yml .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..).\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":196,"startLine":1,"totalLines":196}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QrkaGUiwUQDokYho8eyGGC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
