{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9kWvQe3MSe8nXj4ZJyQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TdtBxqHWZnbKroE8cjK43U","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D17 seen vs. D18+ candidates)\", \"# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D18 seen vs. D19+ candidates)\")\nrep(\"\"\"Updated 2026-10-17 after D17 (1139 ids, 127 members; D17 added AutoHotkey `.ahk`, all modes first try, single T+13 s); gaps\nre-queued 2026-10-18 after the D17-night prebuild (7 built, 1 given up, 1 pending retry).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Updated 2026-10-18 after D18 (1194 ids, 132 members; D18 added Google Apps Script `.gs` + a `google_docs_sidebar` host in a NEW\nmulti-line `SPLIT` carrier; single CORRECT T+54 s after a solve.py carrier patch, TT/Mastery first try). Every queued prebuild\ngap through D18 is built (only python-exec-onion-static given up); the queue below is new.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  The carried solver (`challenges/day17/scripting-fetch-quest/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n  `analyse_v3`; ran unchanged D9-D17) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, on one line, peelable by hex/base64/\n  reverse within 3 layers. The real D18+ risk\"\"\",\"\"\"  The carried solver (`challenges/day18/scripting-orphan-process/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n  `analyse_v3`; unchanged D9-D17) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker data is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, peelable by\n  hex/base64/reverse within 3 layers. **D18 broke the one-line assumption**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` carries no data\n  and the plan sits in a multi-line `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [\"<TAG>-..\", ..].join(\"\")` array (patched in the\n  D18 solve.py; `lib.codec.v3_plan` still returns None -> gap v3-split-array-carrier). The real D19+ risk\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"evidence, find the indicator on only one side\") have never been asked -- yet; rows 66 and 68 prepare for it. D17 is the\n  first prompt naming a SECOND evidence type (network) that was not shipped: the likeliest next twist is that it ships.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"evidence, find the indicator on only one side\", D18 \"source says which process should spawn which, native telemetry keeps\n  its own record; reconstruct the static process tree, catch the child claiming a parent it never had\") have never been asked\n  -- yet. D17 and D18 each named a SECOND evidence type (network, then process telemetry) that was not shipped; the organizers\n  rotate the evidence type daily, so prepare the pattern (declared-from-source vs observed-in-telemetry, find the one-sided\n  item) for network (rows 68/69, built), process (rows 71/72) and file/registry/schedule telemetry (row 74).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack (D17: no host file).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar (D18; D17 no host).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts), D17 back to a Windows automation language (AutoHotkey, sibling of D12 AutoIt).\n  Languages still unpolyglotted: PowerShell v=3, VBA, Tcl, Go, Groovy/Kotlin, R, C#/F# scripts, CI YAML, Makefile/Docker.\n- ~14 drops left (D18-D31).\"\"\",\"\"\"  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts), D17 back to a Windows automation language (AutoHotkey, sibling of D12 AutoIt),\n  D18 a cloud/SaaS script host (Google Apps Script in a Docs sidebar: fake \"Decrypt document\" lure). Languages still\n  unpolyglotted: PowerShell v=3, VBA, Office Scripts/Excel add-ins, Chrome extension JS, Tcl, Go, Groovy/Kotlin, R, C#/F#\n  scripts, CI YAML, Makefile/Docker, Swift/JXA.\n- ~13 drops left (D19-D31).\"\"\")\n# table rows\nrep(\"\"\"| 49 | v=3 marker tags B64 / HEX / HB64 / FRAG | seen D8-D15 | `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` | solve.py `_v3_peel` (hex/b64/reverse, 3 layers) | carried; NEW tag (B32/Z64/XOR/ROT) = **high** risk, peel too narrow |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| 49 | v=3 marker tags B64 / HEX / HB64 / FRAG (+ D18 layout tag SPLIT) | seen D8-D18 | `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-`; D18 `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` with no data + multi-line `[..].join(\"\")` array, real tag on chunk 1 | solve.py `_v3_peel` (hex/b64/reverse, 3 layers) + D18 literal-array join; lib.codec `v3_peel_widen` (B32/Z64/..) built D17 night, SPLIT NOT in lib | carried; next layout tag (array in another language, `table.concat`, `-join @(..)`, heredoc) = **high** |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| 66 | Semantic equivalence\"\"\",\"\"\"| 70 | Google Apps Script `.gs` (+ `google_docs_sidebar` host) | seen D18 | `function onOpen_<id>()`, `DocumentApp.getUi().createMenu`, `HtmlService.createHtmlOutput(..).setTitle`, `showSidebar`, `UrlFetchApp.fetch`, `ScriptApp`, `PropertiesService`, `Object.freeze({ descriptor: .. })`; family `polyglot-google_apps_script` (underscores), host id `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` | carried solver + D18 SPLIT array join; plan `language=google_apps_script`, campaign `GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-<8hex>`, attack parent T1059/T1105/none (not .007); never `clasp`/run | carried |\n| 66 | Semantic equivalence\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| 68 | Source-vs-network reconciliation (declared fetch URLs vs pcap/HAR/proxy/DNS evidence; one-sided indicator) | gap (D17 prompt; no network file shipped)\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| 68 | Source-vs-network reconciliation (declared fetch URLs vs pcap/HAR/proxy/DNS evidence; one-sided indicator) | gap, lib BUILT (D17 prompt; no network file shipped D17/D18)\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"`lib.codec.reconcile({member: plan}, observed)` + `reconcile_answer` (built D17 night; observed = HAR / Zeek TSV / URL list / free text; `refang`, `canon_url`, `canon_host`; answers keep original spelling); raw pcap NOT yet parsed by lib -> `tshark -r f -T fields -e http.host -e http.request.uri -e dns.qry.name -e tls.handshake.extensions_server_name` (INSTALLED) and pass the text;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"`lib.codec.network_indicators(bytes)` (pcap/pcapng/HAR/Zeek/Sysmon 3/22/W3C/squid), `http_objects`, `resolve_chain`, `reconcile({member: plan}, observed)` + `reconcile_answer` (urls/hosts/ips/user_agents/file_names; answers keep original spelling); tshark (INSTALLED) as oracle;\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| 69 | Download cradles / LOLBin fetch call-sites read from CODE (declared side when code and plan differ) | gap (D17 prompt \"the source code says where it would fetch from\")\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| 69 | Download cradles / LOLBin fetch call-sites read from CODE (declared side when code and plan differ) | gap, lib BUILT (`fetch_sites`, `fetch_attack`; D17 prompt \"the source code says where it would fetch from\")\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"URLs rebuilt from concat/format/char-code literals statically (`.venv/bin/ps1`/`js` fold them); gaps `source-fetch-sites`, `lolbin-download-attack-table` | **high**: next step of the D17 narrative |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"`lib.codec.fetch_sites(src)` rebuilds URLs from concat/format/char-code literals statically; `fetch_attack_sites` maps LOLBin -> ATT&CK | med: D18 moved on to processes |\n| 71 | Static process tree from source (who spawns whom) | gap (D18 prompt \"source code describes which process should spawn which\") | plan `steps` dispatch_process / dispatch_language / dispatch_memory / handoff_script + `next_language`; spawn call sites: `WScript.Shell.Run/Exec`, `Shell.Application.ShellExecute`, `Start-Process`/`&`/`Invoke-Item`, `cmd /c`, `start`, `child_process.spawn/exec/fork`, `subprocess.Popen/run`, `os.system`, `system()`/`exec`/`` ` ``, Perl `system`/`qx`, Ruby `spawn`/`%x`, AHK `Run`, AutoIt `Run`/`ShellExecute`, AppleScript `do shell script`, WMI `Win32_Process.Create`, `schtasks /create`, `wmic process call create` | gaps `static-process-tree`, `spawn-api-parent-t