{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9kcdgVGzeXBZDFQjYoo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01753kdgew829jvVWcejo1nq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")\nold=s[a:]\nm=re.search(r\"```json\\n(.*?)\\n```\", old, re.S)\ngaps=json.loads(m.group(1))\nkeep=[g for g in gaps if g['action']!='prebuild']\nfor g in keep:\n    if g['id']=='leaf-ext-list':\n        g['detail']=g['detail'].replace(\".rb .ahk (and\", \".rb .ahk .gs (and\")\n    if g['id']=='family-name-underscore':\n        g['detail']+=\" D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar).\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"v3-split-array-carrier\",\"concept\":\"v=3 marker with no data + multi-line literal-array carrier (D18 SPLIT) in lib.codec\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"lib.codec.v3_plan/find_codecs return None on all 5 D18 .gs files: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` has no data and the plan is `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<8hex> = [\\\"FRAG-..\\\", \\\"..\\\", ..].join(\\\"\\\")` over ~16 lines (first chunk carries the real tag FRAG/HEX/HB64/B64), plus an untagged copy `const encoded_<id> = [..].join(\\\"\\\")` in buildAnalysisPlan_<id>(). The D18 solve.py fix: regex every all-literal array `\\\\[\\\\s*((?:(?:\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\"|'[^']*'|`[^`$]*`)\\\\s*,?\\\\s*)+)\\\\]`, join, also try with `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,12}-` stripped, peel, accept `v=`. Port it into lib.codec and generalise to the same layout in every carried host syntax: Python `\\\"\\\".join([..])` / tuple, PS `-join @(..)` / `[string]::Join('', @(..))`, Lua `table.concat({..})`, Perl `join('', (..))` / qw(), Ruby `[..].join` / %w[], VBS `Join(Array(..), \\\"\\\")`, AHK `[..]` + loop join, AutoIt `StringJoin`/`_ArrayToString`, AppleScript `{..} as text` with `text item delimiters`, MSBuild repeated `<Chunk>` elements, batch `set c1=..` runs. Gate: all D18 .gs members + a fixture battery of D17 plans re-wrapped in each syntax decode to the same plan; no regressions on D1-D18 bundles.\"},\n {\"id\":\"evidence-type-router\",\"concept\":\"classify any NON-script member (second evidence type) and dispatch to its reader\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D17 prompt named network evidence, D18 native process telemetry; neither shipped yet, but the day it does the worker must know in one call what the extra file is. evidence_kind(name, bytes)->{kind: pcap|pcapng|har|zeek|sysmon_evtx|sysmon_xml|sysmon_json|security_4688|auditd|ps_listing|procmon_csv|w3c|squid|edr_json|unknown, reader: lib function name, records: n} by magic/shape (ElfFile header for EVTX, `<Events>`/`<Event xmlns=` XML, JSON lines with EventID/ProcessGuid/event.code, `type=SYSCALL`, `UID PID PPID C STIME`, `\\\"Time of Day\\\",\\\"Process Name\\\",\\\"PID\\\"` Procmon CSV). Then route: network -> network_indicators, process -> process_events (gap process-telemetry-windows/-linux-text), file/registry -> file_registry_events. Gate: every D1-D18 script member classifies as `script` (no false positives).\"},\n {\"id\":\"process-telemetry-windows\",\"concept\":\"observed process events from Sysmon EID 1/5 and Security 4688/4689 (EVTX, XML, JSON, text)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 prompt: 'native telemetry keeps its own record of events'. process_events(data, name='')->[{ts, pid, ppid, image, cmdline, parent_image, parent_cmdline, guid, parent_guid, user, integrity, hashes, event:start|end, src}] from Sysmon EID 1 (ProcessId, ProcessGuid, ParentProcessId, ParentProcessGuid, ParentImage, ParentCommandLine, CommandLine, Image), EID 5 (terminate), Security 4688 (NewProcessId hex, NewProcessName, ProcessId = CREATOR pid hex, ParentProcessName, CommandLine) and 4689; inputs EVTX (Evtx lib allowed), exported XML, winlogbeat/ECS JSON (process.pid/process.parent.pid/process.entity_id), Splunk-style key=value text. Hex pids (`0x1a2c`) -> int; keep the original spelling for answers. Reuse the _ni_sysmon/_ni_evtx plumbing. No csv module (gate).\"},\n {\"id\":\"process-tree-model\",\"concept\":\"build the observed process tree; roots, orphans, depth, chain, pid reuse\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Depends on process-telemetry-windows. process_tree(events)->{nodes, edges, roots, orphans (parent pid/guid never seen or exited before the child started), chains(leaf)->[root..leaf], depth, children(node)} keyed by ProcessGuid when present, else (pid, start ts) so pid reuse does not merge two processes; a 4688 creator pid resolved to the process alive at that time. process_tree_answer(tree, kind, accepted_values, what=) for root/leaf/parent-of/children-of/depth/count/orphan questions, image basenames compared case-insensitively but answered in original spelling. The title 'Orphan Process' = parent missing from the log.\"},\n {\"id\":\"static-process-tree\",\"concept\":\"declared (static) process tree from source + plan\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 prompt: 'Source code describes which process should spawn which ... reconstruct the static process tree'. declared_spawns(plans_by_member, sources)->[{member, parent_image, child_image, cmdline, api, line}]: parent = the member's host interpreter (lang/host_profile -> wscript.exe|cscript.exe for jscript/vbscript/wsf, mshta.exe for hta, cmd.exe for batch, powershell.exe/pwsh.exe, python.exe, node.exe, perl, ruby, lua, AutoHotkey64.exe, AutoIt3.exe, osascript, msbuild.exe, regsvr32.exe for sct, WmiPrvSE.exe/scrcons.exe for MOF, bash), child = next_language interpreter when steps contain dispatch_process/dispatch_language/handoff_script, plus code call sites (WScript.Shell Run/Exec, Shell.Application ShellExecute, Start-Process/&/Invoke-Expression, cmd /c, start, child_process spawn/exec/fork, subprocess/os.system, system/qx/backticks, Ruby spawn/%x, AHK/AutoIt Run, do shell script, Win32_Process.Create, schtasks /create /tr, wmic process call create) with args rebuilt via the fetch_sites literal folder. Gate: every D18 v=3 member yields its edge consistent with its plan.\"},\n {\"id\":\"process-tree-reconcile\",\"concept\":\"declared vs observed process tree; the child claiming a parent it never had\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Depends on static-process-tree + process-tree-model. reconcile_processes(declared, observed)->{matched, parent_mismatch: [{child, declared_parent, recorded_parent, real_parent_if_known, pid, guid}], declared_only (never ran), observed_only (unexpected child), orphans}; match child by image basename + cmdline canon (gap cmdline-canon) + time order; flag PPID spoofing when the recorded ParentProcessId/ParentImage differs from the declared parent or from the process that actually created it (Sysmon EID 1 ParentProcessGuid vs 4688 creator pid, or CreatorProcessId field). reconcile_processes_answer(r, kind, accepted_values, what=) -> child image / pid / claimed parent / true parent / count / ATT&CK (T1134.004).\"},\n {\"id\":\"spawn-api-parent-table\",\"concept\":\"which parent telemetry records for each spawn API (proxy parents) + ATT&CK\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Data table in lib.scripts used by static-process-tree/process-tree-reconcile so an 'unexpected' parent is not mis-flagged: WMI Win32_Process.Create / wmic process call create -> WmiPrvSE.exe (T1047); schtasks/Register-ScheduledTask -> svchost.exe (Schedule) / taskeng.exe (T1053.005); COM MMC20.Application -> mmc.exe, ShellWindows/ShellBrowserWindow -> explorer.exe (T1559.001/T1021.003); services sc create -> services.exe (T1543.003); WMI event consumer -> scrcons.exe (T1546.003); Run keys -> explorer.exe/userinit.exe; Outlook/Office macros -> WINWORD.EXE/EXCEL.EXE (T1204.002); mshta/regsvr32/rundll32 hosts; Apps Script/cloud = no local process. PPID-spoof code cues: UpdateProcThreadAttribute + PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_PARENT_PROCESS (0x00020000), STARTUPINFOEX, EXTENDED_STARTUPINFO_PRESENT (0x00080000), OpenProcess(PROCESS_CREATE_PROCESS 0x0080) on explorer.exe/svchost.exe, PS Get-Process explorer | ... CreateProcess -> T1134.004. Return candidates in order; plan attack= still wins.\"},\n {\"id\":\"process-telemetry-linux-text\",\"concept\":\"observed process events from auditd / ps forests / osquery / Sysmon-for-Linux / Procmon CSV\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Same record shape as process-telemetry-windows. auditd: group `type=SYSCALL ... syscall=59 ppid= pid= exe=` with `type=EXECVE argc= a0=` (hex-encoded args decode) and `type=PROCTITLE proctitle=<hex NUL-joined>` by msg=audit(ts:serial); `ps -ef` / `ps -eo pid,ppid,cmd` / `ps auxf` ASCII forest (`\\\\_` indentation = parent); osquery process_events JSON; Sysmon-for-Linux XML (EID 1 same fields); Procmon CSV `Process Create` rows (Detail `PID: n, Command line:`) and pstree text. Hand-split CSV with a quote-aware regex (no csv module).\"},\n {\"id\":\"cmdline-canon\",\"concept\":\"canonical command lines for matching declared vs observed spawns\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"canon_cmdline(s)->str: strip outer quotes, collapse whitespace, lower-case the image basename (keep args case), drop `.exe`, resolve `%COMSPEC%`/`%SystemRoot%`/`$env:` with the lib.codec _PS_ENV table, remove cmd `^` carets and `\\\"\\\"`, normalise `/c` vs `/C`, `-EncodedCommand`/`-enc`/`-e` -> decoded UTF-16LE text, `C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\` vs `C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\system32\\\\` vs 8.3 `PROGRA~1`, forward/back slashes; split_cmdline(s) Windows (CommandLineToArgvW rules) and POSIX quoting without shlex (gate). Used by process-tree-reconcile and by fetch-site matching.\"},\n {\"id\":\"file-registry-telemetry-reconcile\",\"concept\":\"declared file/registry/schedule indicators vs file/registry/task telemetry\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The daily second-evidence rotation went network (D17) -> process (D18); file and registry are the obvious next. file_registry_events(data)->[{ts, kind: file_create|file_delete|reg_set|reg_create|task_create|service_install, path, value, details, image, pid}] from Sysmon EID 11/23/26 (TargetFilename), 12/13/14 (TargetObject, Details), Security 4698/4702 (TaskContent XML), System 7045 (ServiceName/ImagePath), auditd PATH records, MFT/USN CSV text. reconcile_artifacts(plans, events) compares plan file_path/next_stage/cron_path/schedule_path/service_name/registry keys (canon: HKLM\\\\ vs HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\\\ vs \\\\REGISTRY\\\\MACHINE\\\\, case-insensitive Windows paths, %APPDATA% expansion) -> declared_only/observed_only/both + an answer helper like reconcile_answer.\"},\n {\"id\":\"saas-script-host-route\",\"concept\":\"cloud/SaaS and add-in script hosts after D18 Apps Script\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 opened SaaS hosts (google_docs_sidebar). Likely siblings: Apps Script `appsscript.json` manifest + .gs/.html pairs (sheets custom function, gmail add-on, web app doGet/doPost), Office Scripts `function main(workbook: ExcelScript.Workbook)` (.osts = JSON with the script in an escaped string `body`), Office JS add-in manifest.xml + taskpane.js, Chrome/Edge MV3 extension manifest.json + service_worker / content_scripts, Power Automate / Logic Apps definition JSON, Salesforce Apex `.cls`, VS Code extension package.json activationEvents. saas_host(name, src)->{profile guess, script texts}: unescape JSON-string-embedded code, follow manifest references inside the same zip, then the normal marker/descriptor/split-array readers. Gate: D18 .gs files still route; fixture battery of a D18 plan wrapped in each container.\"}\n]\ngaps2=new+keep\nbuilt=(\"Built by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, stil